This chart compares how families use their income in 1968 and 2018.

Overall, spending preferences have changed a lot between 1968 to 2018. A case in point is that food was one of most spent categories throughout the whole chart. However, food have plunged a lot in 2018. In 2018, leisure and housing have skyrocketed.

Specifically, the percentages have risen to about 19% and 22% with housing and leisure. Transport have increased a lot compared with 1968, with about 8% differience between both years. Household goods accounted for just under 10% in both 1968 and 2018, meanwhile also being the same percentage as personal goods in 1968.

In the year 1968, people almost spend one third(35%)  of all  of their weekly salary in food. However, only 17% was used in 2018. Furthermore, the rest of the categories in the chart mostly obtain the same persentages range, i.e. about 6% to 10%.